# Visita — core rules

Follow [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) and existing code in the same package.

## Stack

- Quarkus + Qute + REST/JSON. PostgreSQL + Flyway (`db/migration/`).
- **Client tracker:** `src/main/resources/META-INF/resources/visita.js` — see [visita-javascript.mdc](visita-javascript.mdc).
- **Dashboard:** Qute template `templates/dashboard.html` + static JS under `META-INF/resources/dashboard/`.
- Repo tooling: no Python; prefer bash or JBang if scripts are added — [visita-tooling-languages.mdc](visita-tooling-languages.mdc).

## Endpoints

- `@ApplicationScoped` + `@Path`. Constructor injection for repositories/services.
- JSON admin APIs: `@RolesAllowed(RequiredRoles.ADMIN)` + JWT.
- Tracking: `@TokenRequired` + `TrackingTokenFilter` for token-gated routes; `@PermitAll` on the resource class.
- Prefer `Response` when status codes matter; records for request/response bodies.

## Data access

- Repositories: `EntityManager` directly; `Optional` for single results; `@Transactional` on mutating methods.
- Query style: [visita-jpa.mdc](visita-jpa.mdc).
- Tracking workflow: `ViewsService` orchestrates `ViewRepository`, `PageRepository`, `DomainRepository`.
- Analytics: `StatsRepository` for dashboard aggregations.

## Tracking headers

- `VISITA-DOMAIN-TOKEN` and `VISITA-DOMAIN-HOSTNAME` — validated in `TrackingTokenFilter`.
- Do not bypass the filter for token-required tracking endpoints.

## Never

- `System.out.println` — use SLF4J.
- Raw SQL in endpoints or services — keep queries in repositories.
- Commit domain tokens or JWT secrets to the repo (dev keys in `application.properties` are test-only).

## When adding a feature

ARCHITECTURE.md §12 — migration → entity → repository → service (if needed) → endpoint → `visita.js` (if client) → tests → dev seed → **update ARCHITECTURE.md**.
